0\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n1-1. Macro Variable Check\n- 10-Year Treasury Yield: 4.71% as of 2026-08-21 [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics]\n- 10-Year Trend: +0.44 pts over the prior year [Actual]\n- Real Interest Rate: not separately sourced [Unconfirmed]\n- Fed Policy Stance: Minutes from July 28-29, 2026 FOMC showed three dissenters\n  favoring a hike and a committee \"far closer to raising rates than the unchanged\n  decision implied\" [Actual \u2014 securities.io, 2026-08-19]. Stance: NEUTRAL-TO-\n  TIGHTENING bias.\n- Fed Funds Target Level: not established in retrieved data [Unconfirmed]\n- Dollar Index (DXY): not retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n- Global Liquidity: not retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n- Economic Cycle Position: Late Expansion with a hawkish Fed; Florida Panhandle\n  home prices already decelerating (below) \u2014 this is consistent with late-cycle\n  stress in housing.\n- Inflation Trend: not directly retrieved [Unconfirmed]; 10Y at 4.71% and Fed\n  dissent toward hikes imply above-target inflation.\n- Credit Spreads: not retrieved [Unconfirmed]\n\n1-2. Regime Classification (Probability Distribution)\n- Goldilocks (Low Rates + Growth):            20%\n- Reflation (High Rates + Growth):            35%\n- Stagflation (High Rates + Low Growth):      25%\n- Recession (Low Rates + Low Growth):         20%\nTotal: 100%\n\n1-3. Macro Sensitivity of JOE (each axis -3 to +3)\n- Interest Rate Sensitivity:      -3  (housing and lot sales are mortgage-driven)\n- Dollar Sensitivity:             -1  (tourism/hospitality; second-home demand)\n- Liquidity Sensitivity:          -2  (real estate transaction velocity)\n- Economic Cycle Sensitivity:     -2  (discretionary second homes and vacation stays)\n- Commodity Sensitivity:          -1  (construction materials)\nWeighted macro impact using the regime distribution: HEADWIND.\nRationale: the two highest-probability regimes (Reflation 35%, Stagflation 25%)\nare both negative for interest-rate-sensitive residential real estate.\n\n1-4. Macro Alignment Judgment: HEADWIND\n- Conviction adjustment: -0.5 step\n- Reinforces a split-entry / limit-order strategy.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n1.5-1. Base Rates\n- 5-year survival probability for an established, FCF-positive real estate\n  operator: >90% [Estimate based on general public-company base rates]\n- Probability a real-estate developer with a large land bank compounds capital\n  at ROIC > WACC for a decade: ~25-35% [Assumption]\n- Probability a \"community/hospitality club\" platform achieves durable recurring\n  revenue: ~30-40% [Estimate; platform-transition base rates]\n- Probability a cyclical housing business sees a 40%+ drawdown within 3 years of\n  a peak: ~30-40% [Estimate; historical US housing cycles]\n\n1.5-2. Deviation From Base Rate\nOur base case assigns a roughly 50% probability of above-WACC compounding, versus\na ~30% base rate. Justification for deviation:\n1) JOE owns ~170,000 acres in a supply-constrained Florida Panhandle [Actual \u2014\n   Fairholme/Fool coverage], giving it a 30+ year development pipeline.\n2) Recurring hospitality + club membership + leasing revenue is now roughly\n   50-55% of total revenue (Q2-2026: real estate $69.6M, hospitality $74.2M,\n   leasing $15.0M on $158.8M total [Actual \u2014 company transcript]), reducing\n   cyclical dependence on lot-sale timing.\n3) Management is buying stock: $32.7M repurchases at an average ~$65.44/share in\n   Q2-2026 [Actual \u2014 transcript], and states it can repurchase $100M+ annually.\n\n1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check\n- Our success probability (50%) vs. base rate (30%) is 1.7x, below the 2.0x\n  red-flag threshold, but high enough to require the above company-specific\n  evidence. No mandatory re-evaluation.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY ASSESSMENT\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n2-1. Business Understanding\nJOE develops and sells residential homesites and commercial land in Northwest\nFlorida; operates hospitality assets (hotels, clubs, marinas); and leases\ncommercial real estate. Its \"virtuous circle\"