iciency:     2  ($32.7M at $65.44, below T0 price; but small vs. market cap)\n2. M&A Track Record:       2  (sold Watercrest JV, no value-destructive mega deals)\n3. Capex Efficiency:       3  (48% residential gross margin, 41% hospitality, 65% commercial)\n4. Rationality of Mix:     3  (development + buyback + dividend + debt paydown)\n5. Guidance Accuracy:      2  (no formal annual guidance; but record Q2 delivered)\nTotal: 12/15\nInsider ownership: 0.36% [Actual \u2014 pack] \u2192 no bonus. Fairholme (largest holder)\ntrimmed 377,800 shares in May 2026 [Actual \u2014 Form 4 via Fool] \u2192 -0 (not\nmanagement, so no penalty per framework, but noted as supply overhang).\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n2.5-1. R&D Capitalization\nNo material R&D. Not applicable.\n\n2.5-2. SBC Treatment\nFY2025 SBC: $0.001B [Actual \u2014 pack]. Immaterial. Adjusted FCF = OCF - PP&E capex\n- SBC = $0.217B - $0.005B - $0.001B = $0.211B TTM.\n\n2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization\nOperating leases $0.002B [Actual \u2014 pack]. Immaterial; not capitalized.\n\n2.5-4. Brand/Data Assets\nBrand value not quantified. Watersound Club membership of 3,723 at ~$10-15k\ninitiation fees (not disclosed for 2026) implies tens of millions in member\nintangible value [Assumption]. Not included in primary DCF.\n\n2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\nGAAP ROIC \u2248 NOPAT / (Equity + Net Debt) \u2248 $116M*(1-21%) / ($776M + $443M - $130M)\n\u2248 $92M / $1,089M \u2248 8.4% (using only long-term debt: ~9.5%).\nIf we add back the low-basis land value uplift, economic ROIC is higher, but we\ncannot substantiate the uplift [Unconfirmed].\nAdjusted ROIC vs. WACC: still below WACC on a GAAP basis, but the land bank is\nthe real asset; the gap is a timing effect rather than a margin-quality problem.\n\n2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett-style)\nOwner Earnings \u2248 NI $116M + D&A $47M - maintenance capex ~$8M - \u0394WC (est.) ~$8M\n\u2248 $147M [Estimate].\nThis is the sustainable pre-growth cash generation of the existing asset base.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3. VALUATION (ENGINE 3 \u2014 HYBRID)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n3-1. Discount Rate Derivation\nRisk-free rate (10Y UST):                     4.71% [Actual \u2014 Trading Economics]\nEquity beta:                                  1.29 [Actual \u2014 vendor in pack]\nEquity risk premium:                          4.50%-5.00% [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran range]\nCost of equity (midpoint ERP 4.75%):          4.71% + 1.29 x 4.75% = 10.84%\nPre-tax cost of debt:                         4.70% (weighted avg interest rate)\n                                              [Actual \u2014 company transcript]\nAfter-tax cost of debt (21% tax):             3.71%\nMarket equity / total capital:                $3,926M / ($3,926M + $443M) = 89.9%\nDebt / total capital:                         10.1%\nWACC (midpoint):                              0.899 x 10.84% + 0.101 x 3.71% = 10.12%\nUSE WACC = 10.0% for the base case.\n\n3-2. Explicit 10-Year Forecast\nBase: FY2025 Revenue $513M [Actual \u2014 pack]; TTM Revenue $548M [Actual \u2014 pack].\n2026E revenue = $580M = +13% vs. 2025 [Estimate; implied by H1-2026 actuals of\n$258M (+15.7% y/y) with a slower H2 due to difficult Q3-2025 comp; no formal\ncompany guidance for the full year].\nGrowth beyond 2026 is [Assumption]: 12% \u2192 4%, fading to terminal growth.\n\nFCF margin derivation: TTM OCF margin = $217M/$548M = 39.6% [Actual \u2014 pack].\nSubtract normalized capex = 5% of revenue [Estimate; company Q2-2026 capex was\n$24.0M for community development/utilities [Actual \u2014 transcript]; some of that is\ninventory and is already inside OCF, so we use a blended 5% of revenue as the\nmaintenance-plus-growth capex charge].\nBase FCF margin = 33% in early years, rising to 35% as mix shifts toward\nhospitality/club and commercial recurring income [Assumption].\n\nYear      Revenue    Growth    FCF Margin    FCF        PV @ 10%\n2026E     $580M      13%       33.0%         $191.4M    $174.0M\n2027E     $650M      12%       33.0%         $214.5M    $177.3M\n2028E     $715M      10%       33.0%         $236.0M    $177.3M\n2029E     $779M       9%       34.0%         $264.9M    $180.9M\n2030E     $841M       8%       34.0%         $285.9M    $177.5M\n2031E     $900M       7%       34.0%         $306.0M    $172.7M\n2032E     $954M       6%       35.0%         $333.9M    $171.3M\n2033E     $1,002M     5%       35.0%         $350.7M    $163.6M\n2034E     $1,052M     5%       35.0%         $368.2M    $156.2M\n2035E     $1,094M     4%       35.0%         $382.9M    $147.6M\n\nTerminal growth = 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 long-run nominal GDP]\nTerminal Value = $382.9M x 1.03 / (0.10 - 0.03) = $5,634M\nPV of Terminal Value = $5,634M / 1.10^10 = $2,172M\n\nEnterprise Value = \u03a3 PV FCF + PV TV = $1,698M + $2,172M = $3,870M\nLess: Net Debt (vendor total debt $573M - cash $130M) = -$443M [Aggregator + Arithmetic]\nEquity Value = $3,870M + $130M - $443M = $3,557M\nShares = 56.93M [Actual \u2014 company 2026-07-27]\nIntrinsic Value (Base) = $62.5/share [Estimate]\n\nSensitivity (Base IV, WACC / FCF margin):\n- WACC 9.5%, FCF margins 34-36%: ~$74-78/share\n- WACC 10.0%, FCF margins 33-35%: ~$62/share\n- WACC 10.5%, FCF margins 30-32%: ~$50-55/share\nThis range is the honest uncertainty band.\n\n3-3. Reverse DCF (What the Market Is Pricing)\nCurrent EV = $3,926M + $443M = $4,369M.\nUsing a 10% WACC and 3% terminal growth, the current price requires either:\n- FCF margins of ~37-38% sustained (vs. our 33-35%), or\n- Terminal growth of ~3.5-4.0%, or\n- A 5-7% lower WACC with the same margins.\nNone of these are impossible, but they are not conservative.\n\n3-4. Land-Bank NAV Cross-Check [Unconfirmed]\n170,000 acres \u00d7 $23,100/acre = $3.93B implied land value at current market cap.\nNo independent appraisal retrieved; no per-acre value by entitlement status is\navailable in the pack. We therefore do not put this in the primary IV.\n\n3-X. Tornado Sensitivity \u2014 Top 3 Variables\n1. Terminal FCF margin (range 30% to 38%): swing \u00b1$20/share\n2. WACC (range 9.5% to 10.5%): swing \u00b1$10/share\n3. 2026-2028 revenue growth (range 8% to 16%): swing \u00b1$8/share\nTop Thesis KPIs: quarterly residential gross margin; 10-year UST; homesites\ndelivered.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n3.5-1. Competitive Response\nIf JOE outperforms, national builders (D.R. Horton, Lennar) will accelerate lot\npurchases and could bid up development costs. Impact: -1 (mild headwind to lot\npricing).\n\n3.5-2. Reflexivity\nPositive: high stock price enables equity-based talent retention and JV leverage\n(Margaritaville JV). Negative scenario: if stock falls below $50, Fairholme could\naccelerate selling, creating a supply overhang. Current state: positive.\n\n3.5-3. Customer Evolution\nEarly adopters have fueled the Watersound community. As penetration increases,\nmarginal buyer demographics may become more price-sensitive. Club membership\ngrowth has been ~4.8% annually (172/3,551), and that pace is unsupported beyond a\nfew years [Assumption].\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4. SCENARIO ENGINE (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nScenario              Probability    IV/share    Key Assumptions\nBear/Recession             25%         $40        Revenue +4% CAGR; FCF margin 28%;\n                                                  WACC 10.5%; terminal g 2.5%\nBase/Fading Growth         50%         $62.5      as in Section 3\nBull/Continued Migration   25%         $95        Revenue +12% for 5yrs then +8%;\n                                                  FCF margin 38%; WACC 9.5%;\n                                                  terminal g 3.5%\n\nExpected Value = 0.25\u00d7$40 + 0.50\u00d7$62.5 + 0.25\u00d7$95 = $65.0/share\n\nBayesian Update:\nPrior: ~30% success probability (base rate).\nUpdate from Q2-2026: record revenue $158.8M, +59% real estate revenue, +37% net\nincome, gross margin expansion, 172 net new club members, 25,000-unit pipeline\n[Actual \u2014 transcript].\nPosterior: ~50% success probability. This justifies a base case, but not a\nbull-case outcome.\n\n50% Confidence Interval: $50 - $85\n80% Confidence Interval: $35 - $110\n\n